S2  Frobenius at s = 0, and the solutions for the constant source -1
  S2a the indicial roots of L_l at s = 0 are 0 and -5/2 (difference not an integer): pass [-5/2, 0]
  S2b (n + 1)(n + 7/2) f_(n+1) = S_n + (n(n - 1)/2 + 7n/2 + kappa_l) f_n: the leading factor never vanishes for n >= 0
        (unique analytic solution given F(0)); f_(n+1)/f_n -> 1/2: radius 2, the other zero of s - s^2/2: pass ratio 1/2,
        zeros [0, 2]
  S2c the constant source -1: F = 2/(8 - l(l + 2)) for l = 0, 1, 3, 4 (exact); at l = 2 the recursion gives F = -(2/7) s
        3F2(1, 1, 7; 2, 9/2; s/2) (exact to order 60) and L_2 F + 1 = 0 at s = 0.3, 0.9, 1.5 (40 digits): pass max
        residual 2.3e-41
  S2c' control: at l = 2 a constant is a homogeneous solution (L_2[c] = 0), so no constant answers the source: F_4
        depends on s: pass
S3  the degree -6 part of P(g_b0 + Sigma_2), exactly
